
Phase 1: Project Setup and Data Acquisition
●	Step 1: Define Project Scope and Objectives:
○	Clearly define the specific writing styles you want to mimic (e.g., specific authors, genres).
○	Set clear, measurable objectives for each stage (e.g., "Achieve X% accuracy in style classification").
○	Incorporate the real-time input and comparison features into the objectives.
○	Identify the core team, roles, and responsibilities.
●	Step 2: Data Collection and Preparation:
○	Gather text samples from your chosen sources (Gutenberg, Reuters, Enron).
○	Ensure the data is sufficient in quantity and quality for each target style.
■	Implement data cleaning:
■	Remove noise (special characters, irrelevant markup).
■	Handle missing data or inconsistencies.
●	Step 3: Set up Development Environment:
○	Install Python and required libraries (NLTK, SpaCy, Transformers, TextBlob, Gensim, Flask/FastAPI).
○	Install Node.js and npm for frontend development.
○	Choose suitable IDEs (Jupyter Notebook, PyCharm, VSCode).
○	Set up version control (Git) for your codebase (both frontend and backend).
Phase 2: Frontend and Backend Development
●	Step 4: Develop Backend (Python):
○	Design the backend architecture using Flask or FastAPI.
○	Create API endpoints for:
■	Receiving text/image input from the frontend.
■	Processing the input (feature extraction, style analysis).
■	Generating text in the target style.
■	Comparing the styles of two input texts/images.
○	Implement the core logic for style analysis, text generation, and style comparison.
●	Step 5: Develop Frontend (HTML, CSS, JS):
○	Design the user interface for the web application.
○	Create forms for users to input text or upload images.
○	Implement JavaScript functions to:
■	Send requests to the backend API.
■	Display the results (generated text, comparison analysis) to the user.
○	Ensure the UI is user-friendly, responsive, and visually appealing.
●	Step 6: Integrate Frontend and Backend:
○	Connect the frontend to the backend API endpoints.
○	Test the communication between the frontend and backend.
○	Ensure data is being sent and received correctly.
Phase 3: Stylometric Analysis and Feature Extraction
●	Step 7: Implement Stylometric Feature Extraction:
○	Implement code in the backend (Python) to extract traditional stylometric features:
■	Lexical: Word frequency, vocabulary richness, average word length.
■	Syntactic: Sentence length distribution, POS tag frequencies, syntactic complexity.
○	Implement extraction of features using BERT embeddings.
●	Step 8: Feature Analysis and Selection:
○	Analyze the extracted features to understand their distribution and importance in distinguishing styles.
○	Use feature selection techniques (e.g., ANOVA, feature importance from Random Forest) to identify the most relevant features.
○	Consider dimensionality reduction (e.g., PCA) if necessary.
●	Step 9: Evaluate Feature Representation:
○	Use clustering (e.g., k-means) and classification (SVM, Random Forest) to validate that the extracted features accurately discriminate between different writing styles.
○	Tune the parameters.
○	Metrics: classification accuracy (target >85%).
Phase 4: Model Training and Text Generation
●	Step 10: Choose and Fine-tune Language Model:
○	Select a pre-trained Transformer model (GPT-2) as a starting point.
○	Fine-tune the model on your prepared corpus, incorporating the extracted stylistic features.
○	Experiment with different fine-tuning strategies and hyperparameters.
●	Step 11: Implement Text Generation and Comparison:
○	Develop the text generation module in the backend.
○	Incorporate your innovative approaches:
■	Custom Control Tokens: Embed tokens like , into the training process.
○	Implement the style comparison logic:
■	Extract features from the two input texts/images.
■	Compare the features using appropriate metrics (e.g., cosine similarity).
■	Classify whether the styles are the same or different.
●	Step 12: Initial Testing and Refinement:
○	Test the text generation and style comparison features through the web interface.
○	Analyze the output for coherence, fluency, and stylistic similarity.
○	Iteratively refine the model, backend logic, and frontend display based on the analysis.
Phase 5: Evaluation and Deployment
●	Step 13: Evaluate Generated Text and Style Comparison:
○	Implement evaluation metrics:
■	For text generation: BLEU and ROUGE scores, human evaluations.
■	For style comparison: Accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score.
○	Aim for:
■	BLEU scores > 0.3 in initial tests.
■	Style comparison accuracy >80%.
●	Step 14: Iterate and Improve:
○	Based on the evaluation results, identify areas for improvement in both the text generation and style comparison components.
○	Iterate on the model, data preprocessing, feature extraction, backend logic, or frontend display as needed.
●	Step 15: Documentation and Deployment:
○	Document the entire process, including code, data sources, and evaluation results (for both frontend and backend).
○	Consider how the engine could be deployed (web hosting, cloud platform).

